        "SRC-001112",
        "SRC-001113"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "December 2025 Council item: Essex asked to amend the Affordable Housing Agreement. Option 1 kept 81 units (27 very low at 50% AMI, 27 low at 70% AMI, 27 moderate at 110% AMI); Option 2 cut to 54 very low-income units (10%). City consultant Economic & Planning Systems put the AHA rents at about $525,000 a year below the developer's assumed rents, a 2.2% reduction in project value. Taking no action leaves the AHA as executed. Legistar shows both amendment resolutions (25-1265, 25-1266) with status Filed.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002202",
        "SRC-002204"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SF YIMBY, November 2021: Essex Property Trust and Infill Land Partners LLC bought the 4.2-acre site, with a 25,000 sq ft warehouse, from Sandhill Land Co. for $33.5 million; the 2021 plan was a five-story, 445-apartment building.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002203"
      ]
    }
